  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Igor Valentinovich tries to fire Fedya and take full control of the kitchen. But Elena arrives with documents proving she owns the restaurant.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Виктор Петрович, не стыдно мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да не особо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Здорово, когда начальство понятливое.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Шеф, Федю уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты что себе позволяешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты зачем Федю уволил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не позволю увольнять моих людей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Здесь я хозяин.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я решаю, кого увольнять, а кого нет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "С меня хватит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Вы все уволены.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я так не думаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Это бумаги, которые подтверждают.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я являюсь владелицей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Этого не может быть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "А пока я буду решать.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Шеф, Федю уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Boss, Fedya has been fired.' Here 'to fire' uses the plural past-tense ending, which also serves for the polite 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты что себе позволяешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you think you are doing?' Chef Viktor combines 'you' with 'to allow' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не позволю увольнять моих людей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will not let you fire my people.' Chef Viktor links 'I' directly with 'not' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Здесь я хозяин.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am in charge here.' The character combines 'here' with 'owner' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "С меня хватит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have had enough.' Notice how 'with' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'enough'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Вы все уволены.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are all fired.' The character uses the polite plural 'you' alongside 'fired', keeping a formal or respectful register. Then Elena responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я так не думаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not think so.' Notice how 'I' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'I think'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я являюсь владелицей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am the owner.' Elena links 'I' directly with 'be' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Этого не может быть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That cannot be.' The character combines 'that' with 'be' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
